  "description": "The Canfield Tilt V1 and V2 (2020–2025) established the foundation of Canfield’s modern mid-travel 29er trail / all-mountain platform. Built around the patented CBF™ suspension and balanced geometry, these first-generation Tilt frames delivered efficient pedaling, confident descending, and the ride composure that continues to define the Tilt platform today.\n\nIntroduced as Canfield’s dedicated mid-travel 29” chassis, the Tilt was designed to be the most fun you can have on two wheels — from after-work rips to all-day epics. The objective was simple: build a 29er that climbed efficiently, remained planted at speed, and maintained the balanced ride character riders expect from Canfield.\n\nThe Tilt was engineered to maintain traction under acceleration while remaining composed through repeated impacts and steep descents.\n\nSingletracks readers picked the Canfield Tilt as All-Mountain Bike of the Year in 2024 — a mid-travel 29er built around the patented Canfield Balance Formula™ suspension. Party up. Party down. Party on.\n\nTilt V1 and V2 geometry reflected progressive trail / all-mountain thinking while maintaining Canfield’s balance-first design approach.\n\nV2 maintained identical geometry and suspension characteristics to V1, with minor production refinements and updated colorways. Ride feel remained intentionally consistent across both versions.\n\nThe Tilt V1 and V2 represent the first generation of the Tilt platform. Rather than a one-off model, these bikes established the geometry, suspension behavior, and ride identity that continues to evolve in newer generations of the Tilt.\n\nFor replacement hardware, bearings, and service components specific to this platform:\n\nTilt Service Parts Collection",
